  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Attempting to fixity check a binary memento is failing when run against fcrepo 6 running in jetty",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "% curl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http://localhost:8080/rest/5bf5ee06-a74e-4a34-80a4-6c2fad2bfa95/fcr:versions/20250519144423/fcr:fixity\nInvalid request for memento at /5bf5ee06-a74e-4a34-80a4-6c2fad2bfa95/fcr:versions/20250519144423/fcr:fixity",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This is despite the fact there is a passing IT that verifies the behavior:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/FedoraFixityIT.java#L168"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "No error is logged normally, but if I add a stacktrace to where the response message is originating, I get the following (line ref is slightly off due to added debugging statements):",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.api.identifiers.FedoraId.processIdentifier(FedoraId.java:542)\n\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.api.identifiers.FedoraId.<init>(FedoraId.java:117)\n\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.api.identifiers.FedoraId.create(FedoraId.java:130)\n\tat org.fcrepo.auth.webac.WebACFilter.doFilterInternal(WebACFilter.java:218)\n\tat org.springframework.web.filter.OncePerRequestFilter.doFilter(OncePerRequestFilter.java:117)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So it appears that during ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "WebACFilter",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-kernel-api/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/api/identifiers/FedoraId.java#L538"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "parsing the fedora id is failing",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " because the ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "afterVersion",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " portion of the id is ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "code"
        }
       ],
       "text": "/20250519144423/fcr:fixity",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " and it can’t handle the fcr:fixity. The integration test may be passing due to webac not being active in that context. In the FedoraFixity controller, the ID it parses has the fcr:fixity suffix removed already by the controller.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
