  "description": "<p>Attempting to fixity check a binary memento is failing when run against fcrepo 6 running in jetty</p>\n\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>% curl -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http://localhost:8080/rest/5bf5ee06-a74e-4a34-80a4-6c2fad2bfa95/fcr:versions/20250519144423/fcr:fixity\nInvalid request for memento at /5bf5ee06-a74e-4a34-80a4-6c2fad2bfa95/fcr:versions/20250519144423/fcr:fixity</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>This is despite the fact there is a passing IT that verifies the behavior:<br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/FedoraFixityIT.java#L168\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/FedoraFixityIT.java#L168</a> </p>\n\n<p>No error is logged normally, but if I add a stacktrace to where the response message is originating, I get the following (line ref is slightly off due to added debugging statements):</p>\n\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.api.identifiers.FedoraId.processIdentifier(FedoraId.java:542)\n\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.api.identifiers.FedoraId.&lt;init&gt;(FedoraId.java:117)\n\tat org.fcrepo.kernel.api.identifiers.FedoraId.create(FedoraId.java:130)\n\tat org.fcrepo.auth.webac.WebACFilter.doFilterInternal(WebACFilter.java:218)\n\tat org.springframework.web.filter.OncePerRequestFilter.doFilter(OncePerRequestFilter.java:117)</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>So it appears that during <tt>WebACFilter</tt> <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/blob/main/fcrepo-kernel-api/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/kernel/api/identifiers/FedoraId.java#L538\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">parsing the fedora id is failing</a> because the <tt>afterVersion</tt> portion of the id is <tt>/20250519144423/fcr:fixity</tt> and it can’t handle the fcr:fixity. The integration test may be passing due to webac not being active in that context. In the FedoraFixity controller, the ID it parses has the fcr:fixity suffix removed already by the controller.</p>",
